-- =============================================================================
-- CivicBrain | V1__baseline.sql
-- The ORIGINAL CivicBrain database (Step 7) as a migration, so a brand-new/empty database and
-- the automated tests (Testcontainers) can be built from scratch:
--   * full schema of the 39 original tables, views, functions and indexes (pg_dump -s of the
--     restored civicbrain_backup, pg_dump 18.6), minus the GDAL "ogr_system_tables" artefact;
--   * reference data only: 8 complaint_categories, 1 municipal_boundary, 23 wards (original
--     geometry - V3 cleans it), 1,113 roads, 25 POIs.
--   NOT included: the 500 synthetic complaints, duplicate results and step13_* prototype rows
--   (load them with db/seed/seed_synthetic_demo_data.sql when you want demo data).
--
-- Existing database restored from civicbrain_backup: DO NOT run this file. Flyway is configured
-- with baseline-on-migrate=true and baseline-version=1, so V1 is marked as applied and only
-- V2, V3, V4 ... run.
-- Empty database: run V1, V2, V3, V4 in order (Flyway does this automatically).
-- =============================================================================
BEGIN;

